You are reviewing one mapped feature slice for high-leverage refactoring work.

Write JSON only to:

<%= output_path %>

Return this shape:

```json
{
  "theses": []
}
```

Each thesis must argue: feature X has architecture problem Y causing cost Z;
refactor A reduces that cost while preserving behavior.

Feature:
- id: <%= feature.id %>
- kind: <%= feature.kind %>
- entrypoints: <%= Array(feature.entrypoints).join(", ") %>
- owned_files: <%= Array(feature.owned_files).join(", ") %>
- context_files: <%= Array(feature.context_files).join(", ") %>
- tests: <%= Array(feature.tests).join(", ") %>

Measured leverage:
<%= JSON.pretty_generate(leverage || {}) %>

Available validation command names:
<%= commands.keys.join(", ") %>

Rules:
- Emit at most <%= max_theses %> theses.
- Cite concrete file paths in every evidence item.
- Include at least one measurable signal in evidence using one of: churn,
  fan_in, complexity, coupling, repeated_dependency, bug_density, coverage_gap.
- Copy the feature boundary from the mapped feature unless you have a concrete
  reason to flag a cross-feature risk.
- Include expected_leverage.score and expected_leverage.breakdown; do not emit
  an unexplained score.
- Include required_validation.commands using the available command names. If
  this slice lacks useful tests, set characterization_first true and explain the
  characterization test needed before refactoring.
- This is reporting only. Do not propose applying code, opening PRs, or
  enqueueing review tasks.
